<div class="wrap narrow prose legal">
  <p class="callout">The short version: we're a marketplace that introduces buyers and sellers of mining properties. We check listings, but we can't guarantee what a seller tells us. Do your own due diligence, never pay anyone outside a signed agreement, and be honest when you use the site.</p>

  <h2>1. Who we are and what these terms cover</h2>
  <p>These Terms &amp; Conditions (“Terms”) govern your use of the <%= config.siteName %> website and services (the “Platform”), operated from <%= config.officeAddress %> (“we”, “us”, “our”). By creating an account, submitting a listing, sending an enquiry or making an offer, you agree to these Terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the Platform.</p>

  <h2>2. What the Platform is, and what it isn't</h2>
  <p>2.1 The Platform is an online marketplace where owners of mining claims, mineral blocks and mines (and people who hold a mandate from those owners) can advertise properties, and where prospective buyers and investors can find them, ask questions and submit offers.</p>
  <p>2.2 We are an introducer. Unless we agree otherwise in writing, we are not a party to any sale, lease, tribute or joint-venture agreement between users. We are not a registered estate agent, legal practitioner, geologist, valuer or financial adviser, and nothing on the Platform is legal, technical, investment or tax advice.</p>
  <p>2.3 No money for the purchase of a property is paid through the Platform. Any payment must be made under a written agreement signed by both parties, and we strongly recommend using a legal practitioner's trust account or a recognised escrow arrangement.</p>

  <h2>3. Accounts</h2>
  <p>3.1 You must be at least 18 years old and legally able to enter into contracts to register.</p>
  <p>3.2 You must give accurate information and keep it up to date. You're responsible for keeping your password safe and for everything done through your account.</p>
  <p>3.3 We may suspend or close an account that breaks these Terms, gives false information, or that we reasonably believe is being used for fraud.</p>

  <h2>4. Listing a property (sellers)</h2>
  <p>4.1 By submitting a listing you confirm that:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>you are the registered holder of the mining rights described, or you hold a current, valid mandate from the registered holder to market and sell them;</li>
    <li>the mining rights are, to the best of your knowledge, validly registered and in good standing under the Mines and Minerals Act [Chapter 21:05] and related regulations, and you'll tell us about any disputes, forfeiture notices, encumbrances or outstanding fees;</li>
    <li>all information, assay results, reserve figures, photos and documents you provide are true, not misleading, and yours to share; and</li>
    <li>you will promptly tell us if the property is sold elsewhere, withdrawn, or if any material fact changes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>4.2 Every listing is reviewed by our team before publication. We may approve, decline, ask for more information, edit for clarity and consistency, or remove any listing at our discretion. We'll usually explain why a listing was declined.</p>
  <p>4.3 You give us a non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to publish, adapt and promote the content of your listing (including photos) on the Platform and in our marketing while the listing is active.</p>
  <p>4.4 Where you don't supply photos, we may show representative images of the relevant mineral, clearly marked as such.</p>
  <p>4.5 Any commission or success fee payable to us on a completed transaction will be agreed with you separately in writing before your listing goes live. If no such agreement exists, no fee is payable.</p>

  <h2>5. Enquiries, site visits and offers (buyers)</h2>
  <p>5.1 Enquiries and offers are passed to the seller or their mandate holder through us. We may screen enquiries and ask for reasonable evidence of identity or funds before arranging site visits or sharing documents.</p>
  <p>5.2 An offer made through the Platform is an expression of genuine intent. It is <strong>not a binding contract</strong> for either side. A sale only becomes binding when a written agreement is signed by both parties.</p>
  <p>5.3 You must carry out your own due diligence before committing to any transaction. That includes verifying title and registration with the Ministry of Mines and Mining Development, independent sampling and assaying, environmental (EMA) compliance, and legal advice on ownership and export rules.</p>
  <p>5.4 Documents, coordinates and maps shared with you are confidential. You must not use them to approach the owner to cut us out of a transaction we introduced, or to peg adjacent or overlapping ground, or share them with anyone except your professional advisers.</p>
  <p>5.5 Site visits are at your own risk. Old workings, shafts, trenches and flooded areas are dangerous. Follow the instructions of the owner and our representatives at all times.</p>

  <h2>6. Things you must not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>List property you have no right to sell, or misstate grades, reserves, size or paperwork;</li>
    <li>Use the Platform for fraud, money laundering, or dealing in minerals in breach of Zimbabwean law (including gold and lithium marketing rules);</li>
    <li>Request advance “viewing”, “processing” or “registration” fees from other users;</li>
    <li>Harass, threaten or deceive other users or our staff;</li>
    <li>Scrape, copy or republish listings in bulk, or interfere with how the Platform works.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If someone asks you to pay money before a site visit or outside a written agreement, please stop and <a href="/contact">tell us</a> straight away.</p>

  <h2>7. Accuracy of information</h2>
  <p>We take reasonable care when reviewing listings, but the information comes from sellers. We do not guarantee that any listing is accurate, complete or current, that any assay or reserve figure will be reproduced, or that any property is free from disputes. Figures such as “proven”, “indicated” or “inferred” are as reported by the seller and may not comply with any international reporting code.</p>

  <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>8.1 To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any loss arising from your reliance on a listing, a transaction between users, the acts or omissions of other users, or the Platform being unavailable.</p>
  <p>8.2 Where we are found liable, our total liability to you is limited to the fees (if any) you have paid us in the twelve months before the claim.</p>
  <p>8.3 Nothing in these Terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded by law, including under the Consumer Protection Act [Chapter 14:44].</p>

  <h2>9. Indemnity</h2>
  <p>You agree to compensate us for any claims, losses or costs (including reasonable legal fees) arising from information you post, your breach of these Terms, or your dealings with other users.</p>

  <h2>10. Privacy and cookies</h2>
  <p>We handle your personal information as described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and use cookies as described in our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these Terms from time to time. We'll change the date at the top and, for significant changes, let registered users know. Continuing to use the Platform after a change means you accept the new Terms.</p>

  <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
  <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of Zimbabwe. Any dispute will first be discussed in good faith. If it can't be resolved within 30 days, it may be referred to the courts of Zimbabwe.</p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these Terms? Email <a href="mailto:<%= config.contactEmail %>"><%= config.contactEmail %></a> or use our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.</p>
